<div id="formulaPop" class="popup"><button onclick="closePop('formulaPop')">Close</button><h3>Formula Sheet - SMS 3451</h3><p><b>Population:</b> P(t+1) = P(t) + Births - Deaths + Net Migration | <b>CBR:</b> Births / Mid-year Population x 1000 | <b>CDR:</b> Deaths / Mid-year Population x 1000 | <b>Rate of natural increase:</b> CBR - CDR | <b>Growth rate:</b> r = ln(P2 / P1) / t | <b>Doubling time:</b> 70 / growth % | <b>TFR:</b> Sum ASFR x 5 (for 5-year groups) | <b>GRR:</b> TFR x proportion female births | <b>NRR:</b> GRR x survival to mean age of childbearing | <b>Life expectancy:</b> e_x = T_x / l_x | <b>Dependency ratio:</b> (0-14 + 65+) / 15-64 x 100 | <b>Sex ratio:</b> Males / Females x 100</p></div>
<div id="glossPop" class="popup"><button onclick="closePop('glossPop')">Close</button><h3>Glossary - SMS 3451</h3><p><b>Demography:</b> study of populations. <b>Fertility:</b> births. <b>Mortality:</b> deaths. <b>Migration:</b> moving in / out. <b>Census:</b> count of all people. <b>Crude rate:</b> rate per 1000 people, all ages. <b>ASFR:</b> age-specific fertility rate. <b>TFR:</b> total fertility rate - children per woman. <b>Life table:</b> table of survival by age. <b>Life expectancy:</b> average years left at age x. <b>Dependency ratio:</b> dependants per worker. <b>Ageing:</b> share of old people rising. <b>Population projection:</b> forecast of future population. <b>KNBS:</b> Kenya National Bureau of Statistics.</p></div>
<div class="topic active" id="topic1">
<h2>Topic 1: Introduction to Demography - Data, Population, Structure</h2><p><b>Estimated time:</b> ~30 minutes | <b>Objectives:</b> Define demography, explain sources of data, describe population structure.</p>
<p>Demography = counting people, and explaining why the count changes.</p><div class='keybox'><p><b>Three drivers:</b> Births (fertility), Deaths (mortality), Migration. Population change = Births - Deaths + Net Migration.</p><p><b>Data sources:</b> Census (KNBS, every 10 years in Kenya), Vital registration (births / deaths), Surveys (KDHS), Migration records.</p><p><b>Structure:</b> Age pyramid - young wide base = high fertility. Kenya: wide base, narrow top. Old countries: narrow base, wide middle.</p><p><b>Example:</b> Kenya 2019 Census: about 47.6 million people.</p></div>
