<div class="topic" id="topic2">
<h2>Topic 2: Fertility - Rates, TFR, Reproduction</h2><p><b>Estimated time:</b> ~35 minutes | <b>Objectives:</b> Explain fertility measures, calculate CBR, ASFR, TFR, explain GRR and NRR.</p>
<p>Fertility = births. But crude rates hide age. A country with many young women will have more births even if each woman has few children.</p><div class='keybox'><p><b>CBR:</b> Births / Mid-year Population x 1000. Crude, easy, but affected by age structure.</p><p><b>ASFR:</b> Births to women aged x / Women aged x x 1000. Clean - compares same age.</p><p><b>TFR:</b> Sum ASFR x 5 for 5-year groups. Children per woman if she lived through all ages at today's rates. TFR 2.1 = replacement level.</p><p><b>GRR:</b> Female births per woman. <b>NRR:</b> GRR x survival to mean age of childbearing. NRR 1 = population replaces itself.</p><p><b>Example:</b> TFR Kenya fell from about 8 in 1970s to about 3.4 today - fewer children per woman.</p></div>
