<h2>Topic 3: Mortality - Rates, Life Tables, Life Expectancy</h2><p><b>Estimated time:</b> ~40 minutes | <b>Objectives:</b> Explain mortality measures, build life table, calculate life expectancy.</p>
<p>Mortality = deaths. Life tables turn death rates into: How long will people live?</p><div class='keybox'><p><b>CDR:</b> Deaths / Mid-year Population x 1000.</p><p><b>Life table:</b> l_x = alive at age x, d_x = deaths between x and x+1, q_x = d_x / l_x, L_x = person-years lived, T_x = total person-years from x, e_x = T_x / l_x.</p><p><b>Example:</b> l_0 = 100000, T_0 = 6500000. e_0 = 6500000 / 100000 = 65 years. Life expectancy at birth = 65.</p><p><b>Infant mortality:</b> Deaths under 1 year / Live births x 1000. Very sensitive to health.</p></div>
