<h2>Topic 4: Migration and Population Growth</h2><p><b>Estimated time:</b> ~35 minutes | <b>Objectives:</b> Explain migration, calculate net migration, growth rate, doubling time.</p>
<p>Migration = moving. It can change a town fast, even if births and deaths are stable.</p><div class='keybox'><p><b>Net migration:</b> In-migrants - Out-migrants. Positive = more come than leave.</p><p><b>Growth:</b> P(t+1) = P(t) + Births - Deaths + Net Migration.</p><p><b>Exponential growth:</b> P2 = P1 e^(r t). r = ln(P2/P1) / t. Doubling time = 70 / growth %.</p><p><b>Example:</b> Population 100000, growth 2% per year. Doubling time = 70 / 2 = 35 years. In 35 years, about 200000.</p><p><b>Kenya:</b> Rural to urban migration - Nairobi grows fast, rural areas age.</p></div>
