<div class="topic" id="topic5">
<h2>Topic 5: Population Projections and Ageing</h2><p><b>Estimated time:</b> ~35 minutes | <b>Objectives:</b> Explain projections, cohort component method, explain ageing and dependency ratio.</p>
<p>Projection = forecast. Not a guess - it starts from today's population and applies fertility, mortality, migration.</p><div class='keybox'><p><b>Cohort component:</b> Take each age group, survive it forward (apply survival), add births (apply fertility), add net migration. Repeat for each 5 years.</p><p><b>Assumptions matter:</b> High, medium, low fertility give very different futures. Always state assumptions.</p><p><b>Ageing:</b> Share of 65+ rises when fertility falls and life expectancy rises.</p><p><b>Dependency ratio:</b> (0-14 + 65+) / 15-64 x 100. Example: Dependants 40000000, Workers 50000000. Ratio = 80. Means 80 dependants per 100 workers.</p></div>
