<div class="topic" id="topic6">
<h2>Topic 6: Demography in Actuarial Work - Pensions, Insurance, Kenya</h2><p><b>Estimated time:</b> ~30 minutes | <b>Objectives:</b> Apply demography to pensions, life insurance, health, explain Kenya challenges.</p>
<p>Demography is actuarial work. If you get population wrong, you get pensions and insurance wrong.</p><div class='keybox'><p><b>Pensions:</b> Need: How many workers pay in? How many pensioners draw out? How long will pensioners live? If life expectancy rises, pension cost rises.</p><p><b>Life insurance:</b> Need: mortality by age and sex, to price premium. Need: fertility, to know future customers.</p><p><b>Health:</b> Need: age structure - old people need more health care.</p><p><b>Kenya:</b> Young population = many future workers, but also many school / job needs. Urbanisation, HIV / AIDS history, falling fertility - all change projections.</p></div>
